      "source": [
        "# Problem: Vanishing/Exploding Gradients Visualization in LSTMs\n",
        "\n",
        "## Problem Statement\n",
        "You are tasked with investigating the **vanishing and exploding gradient problem** in recurrent neural networks by training an LSTM on long sequences. Your goal is to:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Generate a synthetic sequence dataset suitable for demonstrating gradient behavior\n",
        "2. Implement an LSTM model to process long sequences\n",
        "3. Track gradient norms during backpropagation through time\n",
        "4. Visualize gradient flow patterns across timesteps\n",
        "5. Compare gradient behavior in LSTM vs vanilla RNN (optional extension)\n",
        "\n",
        "## Learning Objectives\n",
        "- Understand how gradients flow through recurrent architectures\n",
        "- Observe the vanishing/exploding gradient phenomenon empirically\n",
        "- Learn gradient tracking and visualization techniques\n",
        "- Appreciate why LSTMs help mitigate gradient problems\n",
        "\n",
        "## Requirements\n",
        "- Use PyTorch for implementation\n",
        "- Create synthetic sequences of length 50-100 timesteps\n",
        "- Track gradients at each timestep during training\n",
        "- Generate visualizations showing gradient norms over time\n",
        "- Document observations about gradient behavior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 1: Import Libraries and Setup"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import torch\n",
        "import torch.nn as nn\n",
        "import torch.optim as optim\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from collections import defaultdict\n",
        "\n",
        "# Set random seeds for reproducibility\n",
        "torch.manual_seed(42)\n",
        "np.random.seed(42)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Set device\n",
        "device = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')\n",
        "print(f'Using device: {device}')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 2: Generate Synthetic Sequential Data\n",
        "\n",
        "We'll create a **long-term dependency task** where:\n",
        "- Sequences are 100 timesteps long\n",
        "- A signal appears at timestep 5\n",
        "- The model must remember this signal to make a prediction at timestep 100\n",
        "- This forces gradients to flow back through ~95 timesteps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 2,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Dataset created: 1000 training samples, 200 test samples\n",
            "Sequence length: 100, Input dimension: 2\n",
            "Sample sequence shape: torch.Size([100, 2])\n",
            "Sample label: tensor(1)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def generate_long_term_dependency_data(n_samples, seq_length=100, signal_position=5):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Generate sequences where a binary signal at an early timestep\n",
        "    determines the output at the final timestep.\n",
        "    \n",
        "    Args:\n",
        "        n_samples: Number of sequences to generate\n",
        "        seq_length: Length of each sequence\n",
        "        signal_position: Timestep where the signal appears\n",
        "    \n",
        "    Returns:\n",
        "        sequences: Tensor of shape (n_samples, seq_length, 2)\n",
        "        labels: Tensor of shape (n_samples,)\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    sequences = torch.randn(n_samples, seq_length, 2) * 0.1\n",
        "    labels = torch.randint(0, 2, (n_samples,))\n",
        "    \n",
        "    for i in range(n_samples):\n",
        "        # Set signal at the specified position\n",
        "        if labels[i] == 1:\n",
        "            sequences[i, signal_position, 0] = 1.0  # Positive signal\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            sequences[i, signal_position, 0] = -1.0  # Negative signal\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Add a marker at the signal position\n",
        "        sequences[i, signal_position, 1] = 1.0\n",
        "    \n",
        "    return sequences, labels\n",
        "\n",
        "# Generate training and test data\n",
        "train_sequences, train_labels = generate_long_term_dependency_data(1000, seq_length=100)\n",
        "test_sequences, test_labels = generate_long_term_dependency_data(200, seq_length=100)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Dataset created: {len(train_sequences)} training samples, {len(test_sequences)} test samples\")\n",
        "print(f\"Sequence length: {train_sequences.shape[1]}, Input dimension: {train_sequences.shape[2]}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Sample sequence shape: {train_sequences[0].shape}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Sample label: {train_labels[0]}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 3: Implement LSTM Model with Gradient Tracking"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "class LSTMWithGradientTracking(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, input_size, hidden_size, num_layers=1, output_size=2):\n",
        "        super(LSTMWithGradientTracking, self).__init__()\n",
        "        self.hidden_size = hidden_size\n",
        "        self.num_layers = num_layers\n",
        "        \n",
        "        self.lstm = nn.LSTM(input_size, hidden_size, num_layers, batch_first=True)\n",
        "        self.fc = nn.Linear(hidden_size, output_size)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Storage for gradient tracking\n",
        "        self.gradient_norms = []\n",
        "        self.hooks = []\n",
        "        \n",
        "    def forward(self, x, track_gradients=False):\n",
        "        # Reset gradient storage\n",
        "        if track_gradients:\n",
        "            self.gradient_norms = []\n",
        "            self.remove_hooks()\n",
        "        \n",
        "        batch_size = x.size(0)\n",
        "        h0 = torch.zeros(self.num_layers, batch_size, self.hidden_size).to(x.device)\n",
        "        c0 = torch.zeros(self.num_layers, batch_size, self.hidden_size).to(x.device)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Forward pass through LSTM\n",
        "        lstm_out, _ = self.lstm(x, (h0, c0))\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Register hooks for gradient tracking\n",
        "        if track_gradients:\n",
        "            seq_length = x.size(1)\n",
        "            for t in range(seq_length):\n",
        "                # Create a hook for each timestep\n",
        "                hook = lstm_out[:, t, :].register_hook(\n",
        "                    lambda grad, timestep=t: self.save_gradient_norm(grad, timestep)\n",
        "                )\n",
        "                self.hooks.append(hook)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Use the last hidden state for classification\n",
        "        out = self.fc(lstm_out[:, -1, :])\n",
        "        return out\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def save_gradient_norm(self, grad, timestep):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Hook function to save gradient norms\"\"\"\n",
        "        norm = grad.norm().item()\n",
        "        self.gradient_norms.append((timestep, norm))\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def remove_hooks(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Remove all registered hooks\"\"\"\n",
        "        for hook in self.hooks:\n",
        "            hook.remove()\n",
        "        self.hooks = []\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def get_gradient_norms(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Return sorted gradient norms by timestep\"\"\"\n",
        "        if not self.gradient_norms:\n",
        "            return [], []\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Sort by timestep\n",
        "        sorted_grads = sorted(self.gradient_norms, key=lambda x: x[0])\n",
        "        timesteps = [t for t, _ in sorted_grads]\n",
        "        norms = [n for _, n in sorted_grads]\n",
        "        return timesteps, norms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Model architecture:\n",
            "LSTMWithGradientTracking(\n",
            "  (lstm): LSTM(2, 64, batch_first=True)\n",
            "  (fc): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=2, bias=True)\n",
            ")\n",
            "Total parameters: 21,250\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Initialize model\n",
        "model = LSTMWithGradientTracking(input_size=2, hidden_size=64, num_layers=1, output_size=2)\n",
        "model = model.to(device)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Model architecture:\")\n",
        "print(model)\n",
        "print(f\"Total parameters: {sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters()):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 4: Training Loop with Gradient Monitoring"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Epoch [1/20], Loss: 0.6432, Accuracy: 64.50%\n",
            "Epoch [2/20], Loss: 0.5234, Accuracy: 76.20%\n",
